  "verbalization": "Pravastatin, Rosuvastatin, and their shared mechanism as Hmg-Coa Reductase Inhibitors are linked through a common pathway that involves binding to Slco1b3. The evidence suggests that Pravastatin and Rosuvastatin, both Hmg-Coa Reductase Inhibitors, cause various muscle-related conditions, such as Immune-mediated Necrotising Myopathy, Muscle Swelling, and Myoglobin Urine Present. These conditions are all linked to Rosuvastatin, which binds to Slco1b3. The lowest common ancestor of Pravastatin and Rosuvastatin is the Hmg-Coa Reductase Inhibitor class, and both drugs share a common link to Hydroxy Monocarboxylic Acid. This suggests that the mechanism by which Pravastatin and Rosuvastatin interact with Slco1b3 is likely through a shared pathway involving Hmg-Coa Reductase Inhibition and the subsequent effects on cellular metabolism and transport. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Pravastatin and Slco1b3, mediated through Rosuvastatin, highlighting a potential role in the transport of hydroxy monocarboxylic acids and the downstream effects on muscle function.",
